cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Broccoli in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Broccoli: search results clustering and topic maps in the browser"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Decentralized Science Labs LLC"
version: "1.3.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/GenesisL1/Broccoli"
url: "https://genesisl1.com/broccoli/"
abstract: >-
  Broccoli groups search results into labelled topics in the browser with
  Lingo, Suffix Tree Clustering or bisecting k-means, and draws them as
  zoomable maps (an organic Voronoi treemap, bubbles, a radial map and a
  florets map). It includes a client for NCBI's E-utilities and a PubMed
  search page that clusters up to 2,000 records with no server.
keywords:
  - search results clustering
  - Lingo
  - suffix tree clustering
  - bisecting k-means
  - PubMed
  - Voronoi treemap
  - topic maps
